## Responsibilities

{% JobChecklist %}

- Preparing materials for price negotiations
- Communicating with suppliers and negotiating prices and delivery terms
- Ordering materials and monitoring deliveries
- Working with logistics and the technical department
- Supporting the Commercial Director in purchasing activities
- You will be part of the purchasing and commercial process — not just providing administrative support.
- An immediate start is possible. Training is provided.

{% /JobChecklist %}

{% /JobColumn %}

{% JobColumn %}

{% JobPhoto src="/images/jobs/production.jpg" alt="Employees operating electronics production equipment" /%}

{% /JobColumn %}

{% /JobSection %}

{% JobSection id="requirements-and-offer" tone="subtle" %}

{% JobColumn %}

## Requirements

{% JobChecklist %}

- Good communication and organisational skills
- Care, independence and a commitment to seeing things through
- An organised approach and a willingness to learn
- A university degree (ideally in business, economics or education)
- Communicative English, spoken and written (daily contact with suppliers)
- Independence, thoroughness and the ability to organise your work

{% /JobChecklist %}

{% /JobColumn %}

{% JobColumn %}

## What we offer

{% JobChecklist %}

- A starting salary of CZK 40,000, increasing after the probationary period, plus monthly, half-yearly and annual bonuses
- Opportunities for professional and financial growth
- A full-time employment contract
- 5 weeks of annual leave
- Interesting work at a stable, wholly Czech company (approximately 200 employees)
- Free parking
- Refreshments at work and in our own café
- Dental care at our own modern dental clinic
- Social, sporting and cultural events for employees and their families

{% /JobChecklist %}

{% /JobColumn %}

{% /JobSection %}

